# Agent working memory.
#
# Daily logs are per-session scratch — a running commentary on whatever an agent was
# doing that day, including dead ends. They churn constantly and are noise in review.
# The curated MEMORY.md index is different: it is the durable, high-value summary and
# is worth committing, because a fresh agent reads it at session start and it is how
# hard-won context (a platform quirk, a decision and its reason) survives.
.openhands/memory/*.md
!.openhands/memory/MEMORY.md

# The Debian rootfs tarballs.
#
# A build artifact, not a repo file: ~150 MB of binary in git is a permanent cost to
# every clone, and it would go stale the moment Debian updates. Rebuilt by
# scripts/build-rootfs.sh, which records the exact package versions in BUILD.md so a
# rebuild is comparable. The device verifies SHA256SUMS before extracting.
/debian-engine/rootfs/dist/
